The FakeRunner.run ssh-keyscan branch conflicts: 
- 77fcbbd: `if (command.getFirst().equals("ssh-keyscan")) { scanning = true; if (holdScan) await(() -> scanReleased); return new Result(0, scanOutput, ""); }`
- 4f60ef5: `if (command.getFirst().contains("ssh-keyscan")) { return new Result(scanExitCode, scanOutput, scanStderr); }`

Union resolution: 
```java
if (command.getFirst().contains("ssh-keyscan")) {
    scanning = true;
    if (holdScan) await(() -> scanReleased);
    return new Result(scanExitCode, scanOutput, scanStderr);
}
```

Note: `contains` vs `equals` — the host-key branch changed to `contains` because now the client may be a full path like `C:\...\ssh-keyscan.exe`. Keep `contains`.

